### 6. Edge Cases Analysis

| Edge Case | Handling |
|-----------|----------|
| **Queue fills during burst** | Configurable `maxQueueSize` (default 100). Oldest items dropped with rejection. Caller gets error. |
| **Python crashes mid-batch** | All pending callbacks rejected with error. Caller catches and logs. No memory leak (callbacks cleared). |
| **Gateway restarts with queued** | Memory lost. Acceptable for episodic memory (non-critical). Could add `shutdown()` hook in gateway stop. |
| **Partial batch failure** | Python returns per-item results. Failed items reject, succeeded items resolve. |
| **Timeout during batch** | 2-minute batch timeout. All callbacks rejected. Queue cleared. |
| **Ordering guarantees** | FIFO within batch. Batches processed in order. No interleaving. |
| **Memory leak (callbacks)** | Callbacks deleted on: success, error, timeout, overflow drop. Map bounded by `maxQueueSize`. |

