## 2. Migration Strategy Safety Issues

### 🔴 CRITICAL: No Verification Before Drop

```typescript
// DANGEROUS: Immediately drops source table
log.warn("Dropping legacy agent_events table...");
db.prepare("DROP TABLE agent_events").run();
```

**Fix** - Keep backup and verify:
```typescript
export async function migrateToPartitions(db: DatabaseSync, options: {
  batchSize?: number;
  keepBackup?: boolean;
  verifyBeforeDrop?: boolean;
} = {}): Promise<void> {
  const { batchSize = 10000, keepBackup = true, verifyBeforeDrop = true } = options;

  // ... migration logic ...

  // Get pre-migration count
  const sourceCount = db.prepare("SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM agent_events").get() as { count: number };

  // Get total migrated count
  let migratedCount = 0;
  for (const partition of partitions) {
    const pCount = db.prepare(`SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM ${partition}`).get() as { count: number };
    migratedCount += pCount.count;
  }

  // Verify counts match
  if (verifyBeforeDrop && migratedCount !== sourceCount.count) {
    throw new Error(
      `Migration verification failed: source=${sourceCount.count}, migrated=${migratedCount}`
    );
  }

  if (keepBackup) {
    // Rename instead of drop
    db.prepare("ALTER TABLE agent_events RENAME TO agent_events_pre_migration_backup").run();
    log.info("Renamed legacy table to agent_events_pre_migration_backup");
  } else {
    db.prepare("DROP TABLE agent_events").run();
  }

  // Post-migration: reclaim space
  db.prepare("PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE)").run();
}
```

### 🔴 CRITICAL: No Rollback Capability

**Fix** - Add rollback function:
```typescript
export function rollbackMigration(db: DatabaseSync): void {
  // Drop all partitions
  const tables = db
    .prepare("SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table' AND name LIKE 'agent_events_%'")
    .all() as { name: string }[];

  for (const t of tables) {
    db.prepare(`DROP TABLE IF EXISTS ${t.name}`).run();
  }

  // Drop view
  db.prepare("DROP VIEW IF EXISTS agent_events").run();

  // Restore backup if exists
  const backup = db
    .prepare("SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table' AND name='agent_events_pre_migration_backup'")
    .get();

  if (backup) {
    db.prepare("ALTER TABLE agent_events_pre_migration_backup RENAME TO agent_events").run();
  }

  log.info("Migration rolled back successfully");
}
```

### 🟡 Missing VACUUM After Drop

Dropping tables doesn't immediately free space in SQLite.

**Fix**:
```typescript
// After dropping legacy table
log.info("Running VACUUM to reclaim disk space...");
db.prepare("VACUUM").run();
```

---

## 3. Performance Concerns with View Rebuilding

### 🟡 View Rebuild Blocks All Queries

SQLite has a global write lock. During view rebuild, **all reads are blocked**.

**Mitigation**:
```typescript
private rebuildView(): void {
  const startTime = Date.now();

  // Use IMMEDIATE transaction to reduce lock contention
  const txn = this.db.transaction(() => {
    this.db.prepare("DROP VIEW IF EXISTS agent_events").run();
    // ... create new view ...
  });
  txn();

  const duration = Date.now() - startTime;
  if (duration > 100) {
    log.warn(`View rebuild took ${duration}ms - consider running during off-peak`);
  }
}
```

### 🟡 No Partition Pruning in Query Planning

SQLite doesn't do partition pruning at query planning time for UNION ALL views. A query with `WHERE timestamp >= X` will have its query plan include all UNION branches.

**Mitigation** - Query partitions directly when possible:
```typescript
// For time-range queries, query specific partition instead of view
function queryEventsByTimeRange(startTs: number, endTs: number): AgentEvent[] {
  const partitions = this.getPartitionsForTimeRange(startTs, endTs);

  const results: AgentEvent[] = [];
  for (const partition of partitions) {
    const rows = this.db.prepare(`
      SELECT * FROM ${partition}
      WHERE timestamp >= ? AND timestamp <= ?
    `).all(startTs, endTs);
    results.push(...rows);
  }

  return results.sort((a, b) => a.timestamp - b.timestamp);
}

private getPartitionsForTimeRange(startTs: number, endTs: number): string[] {
  return Array.from(this.currentPartitions).filter(p => {
    const [year, month] = p.replace('agent_events_', '').split('_');
    const partStart = new Date(parseInt(year), parseInt(month) - 1, 1).getTime() / 1000;
    const partEnd = new Date(parseInt(year), parseInt(month), 0, 23, 59, 59).getTime() / 1000;
    return partEnd >= startTs && partStart <= endTs;
  });
}
```

### 🟡 Maintenance During Peak Traffic

**Fix** - Add adaptive scheduling:
```typescript
private shouldRunMaintenance(): boolean {
  const hour = new Date().getHours();
  // Avoid 9am-6pm for maintenance (configurable)
  const offPeakHours = this.config.offPeakHours ?? { start: 22, end: 6 };

  if (hour >= offPeakHours.start || hour < offPeakHours.end) {
    return true;
  }

  log.debug("Skipping maintenance during peak hours");
  return false;
}
```

