### 5. SQLITE-SPECIFIC GOTCHAS

#### 5.1 Views Are Read-Only

The UNION ALL view is **not updatable**. Code inserting via the view will fail:

```sql
-- This will FAIL!
INSERT INTO agent_events (id, type, ...) VALUES (...);
-- Error: cannot modify agent_events because it is a view
```

The current code already routes inserts directly to partitions, which is correct. Just ensure this is documented.

#### 5.2 WAL Mode Essential

With many tables, WAL mode is critical:

```typescript
async initialize(): Promise<void> {
  // Enable WAL mode for better concurrency
  this.db.pragma('journal_mode = WAL');
  this.db.pragma('synchronous = NORMAL');
  this.db.pragma('busy_timeout = 5000');

  // ... rest of init ...
}
```

#### 5.3 Connection Consideration

SQLite has limits on attached databases and query complexity. With 36+ partitions (3 years), the UNION ALL view might hit query planner limits:

```typescript
// Consider a maximum view complexity
private rebuildView(): void {
  const partitions = Array.from(this.currentPartitions).sort();

  // SQLite has limits - warn if approaching
  if (partitions.length > 50) {
    log.warn(`Large partition count (${partitions.length}) may impact query performance`);
  }

  // For very large counts, consider only including recent partitions in the view
  // and having a separate historical query function
}
```

#### 5.4 sqlite_master Query Cost

Scanning sqlite_master is cheap but calling it every maintenance cycle is wasteful:

```typescript
// Cache the scan result
private lastScanTime: number = 0;
private readonly SCAN_CACHE_TTL = 60000; // 1 minute

private scanPartitions(force: boolean = false): void {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (!force && now - this.lastScanTime < this.SCAN_CACHE_TTL) {
    return; // Use cached data
  }

  // ... actual scan ...
  this.lastScanTime = now;
}
```

---

### 6. ADDITIONAL EDGE CASES MISSED

#### 6.1 Concurrent Partition Manager Instances

If multiple processes run partition managers, they might conflict:

```typescript
// Use a lock table for coordination
private async acquireMaintenanceLock(): Promise<boolean> {
  try {
    this.db.exec(`
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS partition_maintenance_lock (
        id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY CHECK (id = 1),
        acquired_at INTEGER NOT NULL,
        holder TEXT
      )
    `);

    // Try to acquire lock (expires after 10 minutes)
    const result = this.db.prepare(`
      INSERT OR REPLACE INTO partition_maintenance_lock (id, acquired_at, holder)
      SELECT 1, unixepoch(), ?
      WHERE NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM partition_maintenance_lock 
        WHERE acquired_at > unixepoch() - 600
      )
    `).run(process.pid.toString());

    return result.changes > 0;
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}
```

#### 6.2 End-of-Month Boundary Bug

Events at exactly midnight on month boundaries could go to wrong partition:

```typescript
// Test this edge case
it('should handle month boundary correctly', () => {
  // 2024-01-31 23:59:59.999 UTC
  const endOfMonth = Date.UTC(2024, 0, 31, 23, 59, 59, 999);
  // 2024-02-01 00:00:00.000 UTC
  const startOfNextMonth = Date.UTC(2024, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0);

  expect(manager.getPartitionName(endOfMonth)).toBe('agent_events_2024_01');
  expect(manager.getPartitionName(startOfNextMonth)).toBe('agent_events_2024_02');
});
```

